//
// Counted 164 by hand. The second real walk, and the one that showed the first
// walk had flattered the detector: here the shipping constants find 153 of 164.
//
// Carried in the HAND, which matters: it is the least damped carry and the noise
// floor is correspondingly loud. That is why this walk can decide the threshold
// RATIO when the first walk (trouser pocket) could not - walk 1's floor never
// cleared STEP_THRESHOLD_MIN_MG, so the clamp decided every crossing there and
// the ratio was inert. Fit against BOTH or the answer is about one pocket.
//
// Walking stops at ~96.8 s and the device is then still until the roam ends at
// 173 s, so any step committed after 100 s is a false positive. The firmware that
// took this capture was still on STEP_CADENCE_MIN=2 and committed exactly 2 of
// them, in one event at t=165.9 s, when the device was picked up to end the roam.
// At CADENCE_MIN=3 that event commits nothing, which is this fixture's second job.
//
// TEN sampling stalls of 398-533 ms, six of them exactly 30 s apart (the pet tick
// autosave) and the rest 2 s or 21 s behind one. 3.9 s of the capture, of which
// 2.3 s falls inside the walking phase. Measured against the local gait interval
// rather than an assumed rate, about 3-4 steps are simply not in this file and no
// detector can find them. That is the ceiling any fit here must respect.
//
// This exists because the detector's constants were fitted to this one
// walk. Without it that fitting is only a number in a commit message.
// Synthetic waveforms CANNOT replace it: a clean spike clears every
// threshold, so every candidate parameter set scores identically on
// synthetic input. Only a real noise floor discriminates.

